From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FE Fates port <port@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:05:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 0025] core: Fire Emblem Fates randomizer: Nuzlocke gate is the
 army, not the camera byte; fallen moved at system calls; graveyard turn and
 name

Round 61. The Nuzlocke frame of 0024 ran only while GameConfigData +0xB was
not 1. That byte is the map camera angle option (CameraBase::
GetGameConfigAngle 0x003E06E0 reads it as 0, 1 or 2; GameConfigData::Reset
sets 1), so a game saved with the default angle (every Birthright save of the
robot) never ran it: the fallen stayed in the army and Casual was kept.

- fates_nuzlocke::in_game: a game is loaded when the unit pool holds a
  player army (force 0, 3 or 4 has a unit). MainSequence ProcSequence::
  GameReset (0x001B6CBC) calls UnitPool::Reset (0x004F6198) before every
  title: forces 0-8 emptied, all 250 units in force 9.
- Nuz::sweep from before_svc: a graveyard person found in force 0 or 3 with
  no map actor is moved to force 4 at a system call, so a battle save's
  fallen unit is moved after its units are read and before the map draws
  it. Every army unit is checked for 1200 frames after a save, state, new
  game or chapter start (Nuz::rearm, chapter change); at other times only
  the units of fallen people seen at the last frame (one force byte each).
  map::Dispos::Data::CreateSortie (0x0039E0xx) takes a person the chapter's
  player-side placement names from force 4 when they are not in force 3;
  that is the Revelation "drawn on the map now" line of round 60, now
  undone at the next system call.
- a death is written only for a person seen alive in the army in this game
  (since the game started or was loaded), so a fallen list from another game
  is never written; the entry carries the map's turn (map::Situation
  *0x006D7ED0 +0xC) and the person's name from the rules' new "names" pairs
  (tools/randomizer/nuzlocke.py make_rules).
- a New Game mode pick closes the Nuzlocke game of the game before (its
  Classic lock no longer touches the new game while the page is open).
- a PLAY RANDOMIZED profile with Nuzlocke on keeps the run
  "profile-nuzlocke" (a patch of no cells + nuzlocke.json, written by
  tools/play/rando.py into the profile's data folder): a New Game answered
  "Randomizer off" lays it (no memory change) and starts a Nuzlocke game.
  No such folder = off as before.

With Nuzlocke off nothing new runs (Session.nuz stays None).
cargo test -p zakuro-core --lib: 197 passed (fates_: 45; new: the gate is
the army, deaths need a living sighting and carry turn and name, the
sweep, a profile with Nuzlocke).
